From 1728ce6516e1ab7ad461c1e1ed8da3621e364d49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:42:56 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(motion): machining3d, multiaxis and quality read
 stock through Stock/Columns

camcraft-motion no longer names Dexel outside tests (M7.3 4/6). The
re-machining masks are Option<&Columns>; the app wraps its prior grid
with Columns::of_grid (borrowed, no clone). Motion's own sims hold a
Stock on the column arm and read through Columns (above, top_over,
top_at) and Stock::measure.

The seam gains the edits motion needs (stock_sim::backend_edit):
Stock::subtract_flat, Stock::cut_chord and Stock::set_tops, each the
old Dexel call on the column arm; the field arm cuts the flat tool with
the spanning flank and refuses set_tops by name. Columns::to_stock
gives the rest pass its owned copy of the mask. quality::measure and
rest_area return Result, as a seam cut can refuse.

Behaviour-neutral: golden_cl, the finish3d/rough/quality goldens and
stock_engine_agreement are byte-identical. Pinned by
stock_seam::motion_names_no_dexel_outside_tests (source scan) and a
bit-for-bit check of engagement_on against the direct Dexel read.

Fixes #587

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
